ure here does not reject every context-dependent mechanism</p></content></shape><shape type="round-rect" topLeftX="48" topLeftY="474" width="864" height="30" presetHandlers="6"><fill><fillColor color="rgba(204,251,241,1)"/></fill></shape><shape type="text" topLeftX="62" topLeftY="478" width="836" height="21"><content textType="body" fontSize="9.8" fontFamily="Inter" color="rgba(13,148,136,1)" textAlign="left" verticalAlign="middle" wrap="false" lineSpacing="multiple:1.15" bold="true"><p>REMAINING TASKS STAY OPEN · NO FUNCTIONAL, SOTA OR RK-G1 OVERCLAIM</p></content></shape><shape type="text" topLeftX="48" topLeftY="512" width="780" height="13"><content textType="body" fontSize="8.2" fontFamily="Inter" color="rgba(100,116,139,1)" textAlign="left" verticalAlign="middle" wrap="false" lineSpacing="multiple:1.15"><p>Source: result 77634740a592 · closeout b401cee135d4 · independent 177/177 · clean 77/77</p></content></shape><shape type="text" topLeftX="850" topLeftY="510" width="62" height="15"><content textType="body" fontSize="10" fontFamily="Inter" color="rgba(31,41,55,1)" textAlign="right" verticalAlign="middle" wrap="false" lineSpacing="multiple:1.15" bold="true"><p>139</p></content></shape></data><note><content textType="body" fontSize="12"><p>RK31 closes the specified known-context applicability analysis and its reporting chain.</p><p>It does not close the full external SOTA, dense-trajectory or unified time-matched tasks.</p><p>Functional untouched data remain unread and RK-G1 remains false.</p><p>The remaining queue is recorded explicitly rather than being represented as completed science.</p></content></note></slide>
